SUMMARY:Hike the Northumberland County Forest
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meetup Location: 101 Beagle
  Club Rd\, Harwood\, ON K0K 44.096\,-78.105**\n\nBeagle Club Trailhead in 
 the Northumberland Forest gives access to 7 loops of single and double tra
 ck trails. 40 km of trails!\n\nGet your hiking boots on and join Big John 
 on a 14km hike though the forest.The **Northumberland County Forest** is a
  sprawling 5\,500-acre\, multi-use forest located in Harwood\, Ontario. Si
 tuated on the Oak Ridges Moraine\, it features 118+ kilometers of trails a
 nd is highly popular for hiking\, mountain biking\, horseback riding\, ATV
 ing\, and cross-country skiing.\n\nBring lots of water\,and lunch and ensu
 re you bring insect repellant as ticks are out in full force.\n(Hat\, long
  sleeved shirt\, and long pants are recommended)
